description:
{panel:bgColor=#e7f4fa}
  *NOTE:* This suggestion is for *Confluence Server*. Using *Confluence Cloud*? [See the corresponding suggestion|http://jira.atlassian.com/browse/CONFCLOUD-49223].
  {panel}

In the Team Calendars admin page, there's a tab that allows you to rebuild space calendars, which allows you to re-run the migration to calendars in spaces. The tab doesn't currently provide any information about what this'll do or why you'd do it. The current title is *Rebuild Space Calendars*, and the accompanying text is *Rebuild Space Calendars*.

Proposed text:

Calendars that have a related space set, or are embedded on only one page, should appear in the *Calendars* section of the relevant space. If the calendars don’t appear there, rebuild space calendars to run the migration process again.

summary_description_acceptance:
Add explanatory text to the rebuild space calendars tab $end$ {panel:bgColor=#e7f4fa}
  *NOTE:* This suggestion is for *Confluence Server*. Using *Confluence Cloud*? [See the corresponding suggestion|http://jira.atlassian.com/browse/CONFCLOUD-49223].
  {panel}

In the Team Calendars admin page, there's a tab that allows you to rebuild space calendars, which allows you to re-run the migration to calendars in spaces. The tab doesn't currently provide any information about what this'll do or why you'd do it. The current title is *Rebuild Space Calendars*, and the accompanying text is *Rebuild Space Calendars*.

Proposed text:

Calendars that have a related space set, or are embedded on only one page, should appear in the *Calendars* section of the relevant space. If the calendars don’t appear there, rebuild space calendars to run the migration process again. $acceptance criteria:$

