description:
{panel:bgColor=#e7f4fa}
  *NOTE:* This suggestion is for *JIRA Server*. Using *JIRA Cloud*? [See the corresponding suggestion|http://jira.atlassian.com/browse/JRACLOUD-37713].
  {panel}

One of the biggest things that customers get stuck on when upgrading is incompatible plugins in their $JIRA_HOME/plugins/installed-plugins/ directory.

We'd probably recommend to remove all of them, upgrade, and then go into the upgraded JIRA's UPM and then reinstall them through the UI.

current doc is this: https://confluence.atlassian.com/display/JIRA/Upgrading+JIRA+Using+a+Rapid+Upgrade+Method

I don't think the current docs covers this in good enough detail compared to the commonality of the problem:
{quote}
If you have installed JIRA plugins (i.e. not included with JIRA), verify that they will be compatible with the version of JIRA you are upgrading to. You can find a plugin's compatibility information from the plugin's home page on the Atlassian Plugin Exchange.
{quote}

summary_description_acceptance:
Elaborate on user installed plugin upgrade procedures in the documentation $end$ {panel:bgColor=#e7f4fa}
