description:
{panel:bgColor=#e7f4fa}
  *NOTE:* This suggestion is for *JIRA Server*. Using *JIRA Cloud*? [See the corresponding suggestion|http://jira.atlassian.com/browse/JRACLOUD-37978].
  {panel}

According to [JRA-34998|https://jira.atlassian.com/browse/JRA-34998], the direct permlinks to comments are now automatically changed to bare issue links by issue navigator. This requires update in JIRA documentation for [Commenting on an Issue - Linking to a comment|https://confluence.atlassian.com/display/JIRA061/Commenting+on+an+Issue#CommentingonanIssue-Linkingtoacomment], which still says that the entire permlink will be displayed.

Affects versions: 6.0 and upwards 
Page and Anchor: https://confluence.atlassian.com/display/JIRA060/Commenting+on+an+Issue#CommentingonanIssue-Linkingtoacomment

{panel:bgColor=#e7f4fa}
  *NOTE:* This suggestion is for *JIRA Server*. Using *JIRA Cloud*? [See the corresponding suggestion|http://jira.atlassian.com/browse/JRACLOUD-38023].
  {panel}

Jira online documentation is incorrect in regard to the behaviour of JQL when searching for issue not assigned to a given user. Since the official position from Atlassian on the topic of [equality being broken for unassigned issues|https://jira.atlassian.com/browse/JRA-25522] is that it will not change then the online documentation should reflect correct usage.

The Jira documentation on currentUser [https://confluence.atlassian.com/display/JIRA/Advanced+Searching+Functions#AdvancedSearchingFunctions-currentUser%28%29] provides a JQL example that will "find issues that were reported to \[sic\] me but are not assigned to me"

{code}reporter = currentUser() and assignee != currentUser(){code}
however this will not return issues that are unassigned. 

It is likely the example JQL should be :
{code}reporter = currentUser() AND (assignee != currentUser() OR assignee is EMPTY){code}

Personally, I would prefer it if JQL were fixed but failing that the docs should be updated.

I would encourage you to update docs with a description of "correct" usage of JQL  where a field is empty as it is counter intuitive that logical operators should behave this way.

summary_description_acceptance:
Documentation misleading when field is empty $end$ {panel:bgColor=#e7f4fa}
