  {panel}

As per the latest documentation [Connecting Jira 6.3.to SQL server 2008|https://confluence.atlassian.com/display/JIRA/Connecting+JIRA+to+SQL+Server+2008#ConnectingJIRAtoSQLServer2008-sql2008driver] and [Supported Platform|https://confluence.atlassian.com/display/JIRA063/Supported+Platforms] we are still recommending JTDS 1.2.4 to customers.

JTDS 1.2.4 has been around for 5 years and was released in 2009. There have been a number or releases since then ( See http://sourceforge.net/projects/jtds/files/jtds/ ) which potentially improve the performance at the data layer and bring features improvement such as Kerberos support, etc.

