description:
{panel:bgColor=#e7f4fa}
  *NOTE:* This suggestion is for *JIRA Server*. Using *JIRA Cloud*? [See the corresponding suggestion|http://jira.atlassian.com/browse/JRACLOUD-41161].
  {panel}

Currently, there are more and more instances/users that prefer to keep their JIRA instances local, and as such should not be able to make any outgoing requests or connections to the internet. 

However, there are some gadgets in JIRA that will actively try to do so. This can cause JIRA to potentially throw errors (as the gadgets are trying to connect to the outside). It would be great if we can have a list of such gadgets, so in the future we know which ones to disable from the get-go.

summary_description_acceptance:
Have a list of gadgets in JIRA that tries to connect to the internet $end$ {panel:bgColor=#e7f4fa}
  *NOTE:* This suggestion is for *JIRA Server*. Using *JIRA Cloud*? [See the corresponding suggestion|http://jira.atlassian.com/browse/JRACLOUD-41161].
  {panel}

